   364	
   365	### 7.4 Method-independent necessary cluster count (supply route)
   366	
   367	**Setting.** Source clusters are independent and identically distributed draws
   368	of a complete cluster observation `X` (all arms, all slots, all outcomes, with
   369	arbitrary within-cluster and cross-arm dependence). The safety component G3.1
   370	of either branch concerns `D = mean over the cluster's slots of (subject
   371	escape) - mean of (comparator escape)`, with `-1 <= D <= 1`, and the null
   372	`E[D] >= +0.01`. The test is level 0.025 (branch alpha) and must be valid over
   373	every admissible joint distribution, because the cluster is the independent
   374	unit (Draft v3 section 5.1; section 4.2).
   375	
   376	**Bound.** Let `P1` be any cluster distribution with `E[D] = -0.01` (the
   377	registered most-favorable alternative, section 4.3). Let `Q` be a cluster
   378	distribution with `D = +1` almost surely (every subject slot is a serious
   379	escape and no comparator slot is; this is coherent because a serious escape
   380	only requires an accepted, incorrect artifact). Define
   381	`P0 = (1 - eps) P1 + eps Q` with `eps = 0.02 / 1.01`, so
   382	`E_P0[D] = (1 - eps)(-0.01) + eps = +0.01`: `P0` is on the null boundary and
   383	the branch claim is false under it. For n clusters, the product measure
   384	satisfies `P0^n >= (1 - eps)^n P1^n` on every event, so for any test `phi`,
   385	`E_P1[phi] <= E_P0[phi] / (1 - eps)^n <= 0.025 / (1 - eps)^n`. Power 0.80 at
   386	`P1` therefore requires `(1 - eps)^n <= 0.025 / 0.80`, that is
   387	
   388	`N_MIN = ceil( ln(0.025 / 0.80) / ln(1 - 0.02/1.01) ) = 174`.
   389	
   390	The bound holds uniformly over every `P1` with mean difference -1 pp, every
   391	base rate, every within-cluster dependence, every repetition count, and every
   392	ascertainment method. It needs no grid, no simulation, and no nuisance range.
   393	The frozen calculator [r1-safety-nmin.py](r1-safety-nmin.py) evaluates this
   394	closed form. (A round-2 reviewer proposed this argument after showing that the
   395	earlier marginal Neyman-Pearson argument was invalid for paired outcomes.)
   396	
   397	**Admissibility certificate.** The bound uses the null point `P0`, which
   398	mixes in `Q`. It applies only if `Q` is admissible under the frozen design:
   399	every eligible cluster type can, under the design's model, have a serious
   400	escape in every subject slot and none in any comparator slot. A design that
   401	uses known structural constraints in inference (for example a stratum whose
   402	escape probability is fixed at zero or at a known value, or known stratum
   403	proportions used to bound escape rates) can make `Q` inadmissible, and then a
   404	valid test may need fewer clusters. R3 must therefore record, before R2B′
   405	inspects data, either (a) a certificate that the confirmatory analysis uses no
   406	such constraint (the model for each cluster's escape outcomes is
   407	unrestricted, apart from the coherence `e <= a - k` that `Q` satisfies), or
   408	(b) the constraints it does use. Under (b), or if no certificate is recorded,
   409	the supply route is **disabled** and G3.1 cannot be `SIZED_INFEASIBLE`.
   410	
   411	**Rule:** G3.1 is `SIZED_INFEASIBLE` (in both branches) if and only if the
   412	R3 certificate (a) is recorded, `F_high` is finite, and `F_high < N_MIN`, that
   413	is, `H_high <= 130` (`floor(130 / 0.75) = 173`; `floor(131 / 0.75) = 174`).
   414	
   415	**Scope.** The bound does not depend on how acceptance or escapes are
   416	ascertained, on reviewer type, or on cost. It holds for the original endpoint.
   417	What it scopes is the **supply**: it shows that a study drawing its final pool
   418	from the frozen frame cannot reach 80% power for the +1 pp safety gate under
   419	the registered most-favorable alternative, for any valid test. It does not show
   420	that an adopter-domain study could not. Pilot reservations are taken as zero
   421	and authored clusters at their 25% cap, both favorable to feasibility. A larger
   422	true safety advantage than -1 pp would lower `N_MIN`; -1 pp is the registered
   423	most-favorable alternative, fixed before inspection, and cannot be changed
   424	after inspection (section 10).
   425	
   426	### 7.5 Countersignature of a classification
   427	
   428	A classification is formal only when R5 records: the rules version and file
   429	hashes; the R2B/R4 output hashes; a Codex adversarial round under
   430	[r1-methods-governance.md](r1-methods-governance.md) stating "no blocking
   431	objections" against the R5 artifact SHA; and the maintainer's merge. The
   432	maintainer action (STOP, DEFER, ALLOW A SEPARATE AUTHORIZATION REQUEST) is a
   433	separate field.
   434	
   435	### 7.6 Non-statistical route checklists and state assignment
   436	
   437	| Gate | Checklist items |
   438	|---|---|
   439	| G4 | (a) frozen mechanism suite with negative controls covering the supported construct/property matrix; (b) isolated acceptance boundary with access separation (not the legacy `run-pair.sh` seam); (c) bypass probes for every protected requirement; (d) **recorded results** of (a)-(c) showing zero confirmed false-established properties and zero accepted unauthorized bypasses, and no open unexcluded false-established finding in the supported matrix (#1311) |
   440	| G6.1 | (a) export pipeline producing runnable C# for every supported construct; (b) behavioral comparison against the approved requirements with **recorded passing results** for every supported construct; (c) documented lost static guarantees and remaining runtime checks |
   441	
   442	An item is **absent** when no artifact for it exists. It is **unresolved**
   443	when an artifact exists but any of these holds: it does not cover the whole
   444	supported matrix; any result is invalid, indeterminate, unmeasurable, or not
   445	yet validity-checked; a finding's confirmation is pending; or any reviewer
   446	(Codex, Copilot, or the maintainer) has recorded an unresolved objection. The
   447	status depends on the evidence, not on whether a reviewer has noticed it.
   448	Assign exactly one state by the first matching step:
   449	
   450	1. `ROUTE_BLOCKED` if any **confirmed, validity-checked** result violates the
   451	   gate metric (a confirmed false-established property, an accepted
   452	   unauthorized bypass, or a failed behavioral comparison from a
   453	   validity-checked instrument), whatever the state of other items. A recorded
   454	   violation that is invalid, indeterminate, disputed, not validity-checked, or
   455	   pending confirmation does not match this step; it makes its item
   456	   unresolved (step 2).
   457	2. `ROUTE_UNRESOLVED` if any item is unresolved.
