   210	    (if rounds remain); or
   211	  - **overrule**: recorded with reasons; R1 is then **not `MET`**, because the
   212	    countersignature requires zero blocking objections. The maintainer cannot
   213	    convert an overrule into a countersignature.
   214	- Rejected `major` and `minor` objections are dispositioned by Claude with
   215	  reasons and published; they do not block.
   216	
   217	## 7. Countersignature format
   218	
   219	R1 is `MET (AI-adjudicated)` only when all of the following are recorded:
   220	
   221	1. A Codex round output containing `VERDICT: no blocking objections`, from a
