   230	   that its model, sandbox, reasoning effort, working directory, user prompt,
   231	   and final message match the committed `round-<N>-prompt.txt`,
   232	   `round-<N>-codex.log`, and `round-<N>-codex.md`. A missing session record or
   233	   any mismatch prevents `MET`.
   234	3. **Merge-time binding check**: on the merge commit,
   235	   `shasum -a 256 -c r1/round-<N>-bindings.sha256` passes for every
   236	   listed file. If any file changed after review, either a new round reviews
   237	   the change or R1 is not `MET`.
   238	4. The maintainer's merge of that PR.
   239	5. No unresolved maintainer overrule under section 6.
   240	6. R0 is `MET` in the merged [gate-state.json](gate-state.json); the live file
   241	   differs from `r1/snapshots/gate-state-at-review.json` only as section 5.1
   242	   ("Live gate state") permits; and the R1 entry is set to `MET` (in this PR
   243	   or a follow-up PR) only after items 1-5 hold. Until then it stays `null`.
   244	
   245	Residual trust that remains after these checks: the maintainer (who has a
   246	conflict, section 4) performs the verification, and the capture operator could
   247	in principle have tampered with the local session store. Both are disclosed.
   248	
   249	Terminal values otherwise: `UNAVAILABLE` (5 rounds without zero blocking
   250	objections, or Codex unavailable), `EXPIRED` (window or cap exhausted),
