   310	## 10. Expiry, revocation, revalidation, and invalidation
   311	
   312	**Revalidation.** Before a gate starts, before each data access, and
   313	immediately before closure, the acting agent checks, and records in the gate
   314	record with the date and the commit SHA of gate-state.json it read:
   315	
   316	1. R0: current value `MET`, not expired, not revoked, and active authority
   317	   has not ended (below);
   318	2. for **each** gate in the transitive prerequisite closure of the acting
   319	   gate (for example R5 checks R0, R1, R2A′, R3, R2B′, and R4, not only R4):
   320	   its current value is `MET`
   321	   in [gate-state.json](gate-state.json); any expiry stated in its own record
   322	   has not passed; no withdrawal, exclusion, license change, or invalidation
   323	   affecting it is recorded in its record, in Section 13, or on #1370 after
   324	   its `MET` date; and the output version (commit SHA) it relied on is the one
   325	   still recorded as current;
   326	3. the cumulative spend and hours are under their caps.
   327	
   328	Any failed check stops the work. If a check finds that a prerequisite's
   329	authority or input has lapsed while gate-state.json still shows `MET` (stale
   330	state), the agent records the finding in the active PR, and work resumes only
   331	after the maintainer has merged the invalidation update under the rule below.
   332	
   333	**Completion and end of authority.** The inquiry is **complete** when R5 is
   334	dispositioned (its value recorded in gate-state.json and merged). Active
   335	authority ends at the earlier of completion and 2026-10-29 23:59 UTC.
   336	
